  "arrangerNotes": "Refrain, vocal line, transcribed by visual reading of the original 1927 T. B. Harms sheet music (scan and LilyPond transcription saved in scores/b10/), key E flat major, 4/4 (durations in quarter-note beats), second ending. Melody only: the 1927 lyrics are written in dialect, so the tune is given without words. Simplification: the three A naturals in the middle section ('Tote dat barge', 'Lift dat bale', 'git a little drunk', a raised 4th) are played as 4 (A flat). Range low 5 to high 3. D drum: the notes as written. C drum (no high 2 or 3): the last phrase, from 'skeered of dyin'', is played an octave lower, so the closing climax sits in the middle octave. C and D arrangements differ where noted above (each fits its own drum).",
  "verified": true
}
